    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_bfd5912a",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: self-deprecating humor; overall-intent-description: The meme uses a juxtaposition of two images: a man in a professional setting looking thoughtful, and a woman with a skeptical expression. The text reads, \"i don't always speak my mind, but when i do, i sound like a damn idiot.\" The overall intent is self-deprecating humor, where the speaker acknowledges their tendency to say things that sound foolish when they do speak up. There is no indication of toxicity, harmful content, or targeting of any specific group based on protected characteristics. The humor is personal and relatable, not abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic. The visual elements support the textual message by showing expressions of contemplation and skepticism, reinforcing the idea of internal conflict or self-doubt about speaking one's mind.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_9a8bf23e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
